    "The .data and bss stay ROM-owned and are reached by extern, as the one-function sources did; the unit owns its .text, its static initializer (.init) and the .ctors word.",
    "Folded from 117 sources: the link module's 38 (#5389) and the wireless layer's 79 (83 functions). The file is C++ for Memory::Allocate (func_0203e20c, func_0203f604, func_020408b0) and the file-scope EmptyInit object; every function keeps C linkage inside one extern \"C\" block.",
    "No pragma. func_0203e20c's step 3 reduces its accepted-children count to a result it never reads, as step 5 does with the result it loops on; the optimiser deletes only that last assignment, which keeps the count (the cartridge's addeq/andeq). WFSi_LoadTables starts its size total at 0 and adds the leading word, which keeps the cartridge's add from the zeroed counter.",
    "Absorbed arm9/func_02040384 (intact-object): its __sinit_func_02040384.cpp/.p__sinit_func_02040384.cpp are renamed for this file. sEmptyInit stays static and deadstripped, so data_020a0df4 stays a gap.",
    "func_0203e0ac and the tail of func_0203e20c copy the local input record into all four player records with chained field assignments. PlayerInputRecord.inputYaw is u16: both copies read it back with ldrh."
